## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design precise resource accounting at OS level, handle races, and ensure fairness under contention.

## Key Concepts
- Per-core accounting, PMU counters, energy deltas
- Quanta windows and atomic updates
- Throttling policies and starvation avoidance
- I/O crediting and test methodologies

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo sketch: per-task energy accounting
struct core_state { long long quota; atomic_ll energy_acc; pthread_mutex_t lock; };
void on_dispatch(Task *t){
  long long d = estimate_energy(t); // from PMU
  atomic_add(&t->energy, d);
  if (atomic_read(&t->energy) > t->quota) throttle(t);
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you calibrate energy deltas across heterogeneous cores?
- How would you extend this to NUMA and turbo-frequency changes?

